# The axiom-audit ledger (REQ-HONESTY-AXIOMS-001; `cargo xtask check axioms-audit`).
#
# What the CHECKERS say, read from the compiled objects -- not from the source:
#
#   rocq-set <set> <axiom> <ID>          a named axiom set, listed once
#   rocq-lib <module> theory <item> <ID> set-predicative | set-impredicative,
#                                        rewrite-rules-disallowed | -allowed
#   rocq-lib <module> uses <set> <ID>    the library's axioms include the set
#   rocq-lib <module> axiom <name> <ID>  one more axiom (an Admitted lemma is one)
#   rocq-lib <module> bypass <kind> <name> <ID>
#                                        type-in-type | unsafe-fixpoint | positivity
#   lean-mod <module> constants N theorems M unreplayed K <ID>
#   lean-axiom <module> <axiom> <N> <ID> N of the module's constants depend on it
#
# Rocq rows are per LIBRARY (`rocqchk -o`: everything the library loads), an
# over-approximation of what any one theorem uses. A library's axioms must
# equal the union of the sets it uses and its own axiom rows, exactly.
#
# mode = equality: any difference fails -- a new axiom AND one that went away.
# The ratchet (shrink-only after the v0.11.0 tag, as trust-ledger) is not
# implemented in this gate yet; `mode = shrink-only` and `admit` rows are
# refused until it is.
#
# Regenerate rows with `cargo xtask axioms-audit --write --id <ARTIFACT-ID>`
# (unchanged rows keep their ID).

mode = equality
baseline = none
